course: dictionary
lesson: 8159
title: Spotting resemblance
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: A resemblance is a way in which things are alike. When two things look alike, or share a feature, there is a resemblance between them. «You bear a strong resemblance to your dad» means you look like him, perhaps with his eyes or his smile.
explain: Resemblance is a noun, and its plural is resemblances. Look out for phrases like «bear a resemblance to», «a strong resemblance» and «family resemblance». Each one tells you that two things are similar in some way.
explain: In the story, Toad arranges bedroom chairs «in rude resemblance of a motor-car». The chairs are not really a car. The words in rude resemblance tell you he set them out so they looked like one. So resemblance means being similar to something.
fact: Resemblance means being similar to someone or something, especially in how they look.
fact: A resemblance can also be any way in which things are similar, not only how they look.
fact: «A strong family resemblance» means relatives look alike.
fact: In maths, similar shapes bear a resemblance: they have the same shape but a different size.
fact: In science, children resemble their parents because of genes.
exercise: «You bear a strong resemblance to your dad.» What does resemblance mean here? | Liking the same food | Being far away from home | *Looking alike | Being very tall
exercise: Toad arranges chairs «in rude resemblance of a motor-car». What are the chairs made to look like? | A horse and cart | A bedroom | A castle on a hill | *A motor-car
exercise: Two triangles have the same shape but one is much bigger. What do they bear? | *A resemblance | A length | A colour | A problem
test: Which phrase means that two people look very similar? | A loud noise | A long journey | A heavy load | *A close resemblance
test: Which word means a way in which things are similar? | Distance | Solution | *Resemblance | Difference
exam: Which sentence uses resemblance correctly? | *Ella bears a close resemblance to her mum | Ella resemblances her mum wildly today | Ella resemblance the bus quickly every day | Ella is very resemblance at the bus stop
